    "text": "```python\ndef starts_one_ends(n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Given a positive integer n, return the count of the n-digit n-digit numbers\n    that either start or end with 1.\n    \"\"\"\n    count = 0\n\n    for i in range(1 << n) + 1):\n        count += 1\n\n    return count\n\n\n```\n\nHere's how the function works:\n\n1. It iterates numbers from 1 to \\( 10^n \\), which represents all n-digit numbers with 1.\n2. It increments the count for each of these numbers that either start or end with 1.\n3. Finally, it returns the count of such numbers.",
